---
const termuxSteps = [
  {
    label: "deps",
    code: "pkg update && pkg install python libxml2 libxslt libjpeg-turbo",
  },
  { label: "pip", code: "pip install worldnews-cli" },
  { label: "voice", code: 'pip install "worldnews-cli[voice]"' },
  { label: "extras", code: "pkg install termux-api ffmpeg" },
  { label: "run", code: "python -m worldnews" },
];

const widths = [
  { cols: "100+", layout: "Sidebar + list + reader" },
  { cols: "84-99", layout: "List first; Enter opens the reader" },
  { cols: "under 84", layout: "Single column; Enter = reader, Esc = list" },
  { cols: "under 56", layout: "Compact rows and short key hints" },
];
---

<section class="section mobile" id="mobile">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Mobile</p>
      <h2>Phones and small screens</h2>
      <p>
        This is a terminal app, not a store app. On Android it usually runs inside Termux. On a
        narrow screen the layout collapses to list-or-reader instead of three panes.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mobile-block reveal">
      <h3>Android (Termux)</h3>
      <ol class="mobile-steps">
        <li>Install <a href="https://termux.dev/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Termux</a> from its official site or F-Droid (not a random Play Store clone).</li>
        <li>Open Termux and run the commands below.</li>
        <li>Prefer <code>python -m worldnews</code> if <code>worldnews</code> is missing from PATH.</li>
      </ol>
      <ul class="cmd-list">
        {
          termuxSteps.map((c) => (
            <li class="cmd-row">
              <span class="cmd-label mono">{c.label}</span>
              <code class="cmd-code">{c.code}</code>
              <button
                type="button"
                class="cmd-copy"
                data-copy={c.code}
                aria-label={`Copy ${c.label} command`}>Copy</button
              >
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="mobile-note">
        <code>termux-api</code> helps open links in the system browser. <code>ffmpeg</code> helps some
        voice playback paths.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mobile-block reveal">
      <h3>iOS and other options</h3>
      <p>
        There is no App Store build. On iOS, people sometimes use a-Shell or iSH with Python and pip,
        but setup is fiddly and packages can fail. A steadier path is SSH (JuiceSSH, ConnectBot, or
        similar) into a machine that already has <code>worldnews</code> installed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mobile-block reveal" id="mobile-limits">
      <h3>Limitations</h3>
      <ul class="limit-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Not a native mobile UI.</strong> You are in a terminal. Touch works for taps, but
          the app is keyboard-first.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Width changes the layout.</strong> Below about 84 columns you get one column at a
          time. Enter opens the reader; Esc goes back to the list.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Complex scripts.</strong> Malayalam, Hindi, Arabic, and similar scripts often
          overlap in cell-grid terminals. Default safe mode hides those glyphs in the TUI; press
          <code>o</code> to read in a browser, or <code>t</code> to hear the story.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Fonts matter.</strong> In Termux, install a font that covers the languages you
          care about (for example Noto). Without that, more characters look broken.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Install weight.</strong> You need Python plus native libs (<code>libxml2</code>,
          <code>libxslt</code>, JPEG). First install can take a while on older phones.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Battery and data.</strong> Fetching feeds uses the network. Speak and AI features
          add more work when you turn them on.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="width-table" role="table" aria-label="Terminal width layout">
        <div class="width-row width-head" role="row">
          <span role="columnheader">Columns</span>
          <span role="columnheader">Layout</span>
        </div>
        {
          widths.map((w) => (
            <div class="width-row" role="row">
              <span class="mono" role="cell">
                {w.cols}
              </span>
              <span role="cell">{w.layout}</span>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .mobile-block {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    max-width: 44rem;
  }

  .mobile-block h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  .mobile-block p,
  .mobile-steps li {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .mobile-steps {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .mobile-steps a {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .mobile-note {
    margin-top: 0.85rem;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--mute);
  }

  .cmd-list {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .cmd-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr auto;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .cmd-label {
    color: var(--mute);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .cmd-code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: clamp(0.75rem, 1.3vw, 0.92rem);
    background: transparent;
    word-break: break-all;
  }

  .cmd-copy {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 0.45rem 0.7rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .cmd-copy:hover,
  .cmd-copy.is-copied {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    border-color: var(--ink);
  }

  .limit-list {
    margin: 0 0 1.25rem;
    padding-left: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .limit-list li {
    margin-bottom: 0.65rem;
  }

  .width-table {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .width-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 7rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.7rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .width-head {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--mute);
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .cmd-row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    }
    .cmd-label {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
    .width-row {
      grid-template-columns: 5.5rem 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("#mobile [data-copy]").forEach((btn) => {
    btn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      const text = btn.dataset.copy || "";
      try {
        await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
        btn.classList.add("is-copied");
        btn.textContent = "Copied";
        window.setTimeout(() => {
          btn.classList.remove("is-copied");
          btn.textContent = "Copy";
        }, 1600);
      } catch {
        btn.textContent = "Fail";
      }
    });
  });
</script>
